            <ArticleTitle>Interactions between vagal afferent nerve subtypes mediating cough.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>187-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The cough reflex is initiated through activation of vagal afferent nerves. Rapidly adapting receptors fulfill all criteria for the afferents subserving the cough reflex. Bronchopulmonary C-fibres may also initiate cough when activated. C-fibre-mediated cough may depend upon ongoing or initiated activity in rapidly adapting receptors. The interaction between airways C-fibres and rapidly adapting receptors may occur at sites in the periphery or in the brainstem. C-fibre mediated cough must also overcome a coincident inhibitory effect of C-fibre activation on cough, an inhibitory effect that becomes prominent under general anesthaesia.</AbstractText>
